@host = http://localhost:5036
@annaLindqvist = 30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@johanBergPlumber = 40000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Create a request: Anna Lindqvist, Tallbacken 1101 -> 201
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "residentId": "{{annaLindqvist}}",
  "title": "Kitchen tap leaking",
  "description": "Water drips from the base of the kitchen tap even when it is fully closed.",
  "category": "Plumbing",
  "priority": "Normal"
}

### Get it back -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### List submitted requests, first page -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests?status=Submitted&page=1&pageSize=20

### Triage it -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Triaged"
}

### Assign Johan Berg, plumber -> 200, status becomes Assigned
PATCH {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/assignment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "technicianId": "{{johanBergPlumber}}"
}

### FAILS: missing title, category given as a number -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "residentId": "{{annaLindqvist}}",
  "description": "No title, and a number where a category name belongs.",
  "category": 1,
  "priority": "Normal"
}

### FAILS: resident does not exist -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "residentId": "30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099",
  "title": "Nobody lives here",
  "description": "This resident id is not seeded.",
  "category": "Other",
  "priority": "Low"
}

### FAILS: request does not exist -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### FAILS: page size above the maximum -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/maintenance-requests?pageSize=500
